# Normalise line endings so a clone is byte-identical on every platform, rather
# than depending on each contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Text is stored as
# LF in the repository and checked out in the platform's native form.
#
# The tables matter most here: the solver writes them through a text-mode
# stream, so a Windows run produces CRLF and a Linux run produces LF. Without
# this, regenerating a table on the other platform would show every line as
# changed. The tools that read them are line-ending agnostic either way.

* text=auto

*.cpp     text
*.hpp     text
*.py      text
*.md      text
*.tsv     text
*.cff     text
*.txt     text
LICENSE   text
CMakeLists.txt   text
.clang-format    text
.gitattributes   text
.gitignore       text

*.pdf     binary
